( bounda_baseline_correction_parameters given in the input (manual 6.20),
  F5 T5 U9: they are used instead of the fit. p = 0.5 on [0,1], so the
  acceleration is 1.5, v(1) = 1.5 and x(1) = 0.1*0.15*(1+...+10) = 0.825.
  Same as the Professional 02-08-2026 for this case: every table point
  after time_start gets +0.5, the first point is not corrected there. )
echo -no
number_of_space_dimensions 1
materi_acceleration
materi_velocity
materi_displacement
end_initia
inertia_apply -yes
node 1  0
node 2  1
element 1  -truss 1 2
group_type 0  -truss
group_truss_area 0  1.0
group_truss_elasti_young 0  1.0
group_truss_density 0  2.0
bounda_dof  10  1 -accx
bounda_time 10  0. 1.  0.5 1.  1. 1.  2. 0.
bounda_baseline_correction 0. 1.
bounda_baseline_correction_parameters 10  0.5 0. 0.
control_timestep 10  0.1 1.
target_item  0  -node_dof 1 -velx
target_value 0  1.5 1.e-10
target_item  1  -node_dof 1 -disx
target_value 1  0.825 1.e-10
target_item  2  -bounda_baseline_correction_parameters 10 0
target_value 2  0.5 1.e-10
end_data
